4. MULTI-CONTAINER ORCHESTRATION (`docker-compose.yml`)
================================================================================
`docker-compose.yml` connects three containers (`mysql_db`, `zaika_backend`, and `zaika_frontend`) over a shared Docker network, including a `healthcheck` so FastAPI waits until MySQL is completely ready before creating tables.

```yaml
version: "3.9"

services:
  mysql_db:
    image: mysql:8.0
    container_name: zaika_mysql
    restart: always
    environment:
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: rootpassword
      MYSQL_DATABASE: zaika_db
    ports:
      - "3306:3306"
    volumes:
      - mysql_data:/var/lib/mysql
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "mysqladmin", "ping", "-h", "localhost", "-prootpassword"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5

  zaika_backend:
    build:
      context: ./backend
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    container_name: zaika_api
    restart: always
    depends_on:
      mysql_db:
        condition: service_healthy
    environment:
      MYSQL_URL: mysql+pymysql://root:rootpassword@mysql_db:3306/zaika_db
      SQLITE_URL: sqlite:///./audit_logs.db
      SECRET_KEY: zaika_super_secret_jwt_key_2026
    ports:
      - "8000:8000"

  zaika_frontend:
    build:
      context: ./frontend
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    container_name: zaika_ui
    restart: always
    depends_on:
      - zaika_backend
    environment:
      API_BASE_URL: http://zaika_backend:8000
    ports:
      - "8501:8501"

volumes:
  mysql_data:
```

Useful Docker Commands Cheat Sheet:
- Build and launch entire system: `docker-compose up --build -d`
- Check running container status: `docker-compose ps`
- View live FastAPI backend logs: `docker-compose logs -f zaika_backend`
- Stop and clean up containers: `docker-compose down`

